{
  "//": "Weapon inspect motions (Docs/forge-skin/PLAN.md §4.14; the format in full: Mods/ForgeSkin/DEVELOPERS.md). Times are the motion's own seconds; a kind's feel.slow stretches them. feel, per kind: the item's weight on the wrist that carries it over the keys (a spring of f hertz and zeta damping driven by the keys' own acceleration: the item hangs back as the hand starts and goes past as it stops; carry how much of that shows, wind the degrees it draws back before a large turn), hit [degrees, metres] the push of a knock, spin the most degrees a second it turns while held, slow. The grip hand's fingers are not keyed: its thumb and three fingers keep the game's own grip (the one finger pose that lies on its surface) and open only for a twirl or a toss, closing after the catch; its index finger leaves the trigger for the look and lies along the side of the gun (in the guard again for a twirl; in a motion from the hold it keeps the game's). The off hand's fingers close as far as its key says or until they come to a mesh of the gun; under the gun they are the game's own unless the key gives a shape. gun: turn, tilt, roll (degrees from the gun held level and ahead; in a motion with \"from\": \"hold\", as melee weapons have, from the hold the game has the item in, about the view's up, right and forward; with \"palm\": true from that hold with the grip hand's palm turned up, where an item is thrown from and caught), at [x, y] (the bounds centre in the half view), fill, rise, spin (a twirl between two keys, or whole turns end over end of a toss), flip (whole turns of a toss about the item's length), toss (metres up: the key is the catch; release, wind-up, follow-through, catch and sink are solved from toss and g), hold stock, windup, settle, through (a key the gun only passes: no dwell asked of it), hit (arriving is a knock), cue. hand (the off hand: it supports the gun from below, is out of the view, or works a part; it never takes the grip): on grip | away | under (along) | side | top | muzzle (along) | node | mag | open; node and mag take face (left, right, top, bottom of the part's drawn box), at [u along the gun, v across the face], offset [out, across, along] metres, spin (degrees the hand is turned on the face); a mag key with no at holds the magazine on its own box: with no face by its side (its back edge at the web of the thumb low down, the four fingers along its left face, the thumb round onto its right, the last two fingers under its base, nothing near its top; spin lifts the fingers toward its top), with face bottom, or where it is wider than the hand takes so, by its base (the base on the palm, the fingers up its front, the thumb up its left face); the offset of either is [to the magazine's left, up it, to its front]; tips on a node key puts the pads of the index and middle fingers on the point instead of the palm; fingers [thumb, index, middle, ring, pinky]; cue. parts: node (a name, or names of which the gun's first drawn one is taken; @mag, @round), about, optional, follow, symmetry (rest rolls to the nearest whole of it); keys move, out, clear (out as a share of the part's own height), turn, show, ease (in | out | spring, bounce), carry { at, dist, roll, tip } (held in the view: tip the degrees its top is turned from straight at the eye toward up), cue. A cue is played through sounds.cues as roles, each role resolved on the gun's own reload and fire sounds (match), else its default by kind. kinds: pools (a gun's kind lists the look, the toss, the magazine check and its own motions; a motion whose part a gun does not have is left out for that gun and logged once). gear: offline gear id -> pool and motions; each press plays one at random, never the last. fallback: the pool by measured length; entries with \"melee\": true are for melee weapons. default: the pool of anything held that is neither a gun nor a melee weapon (a tool, a pack, another mod's item) and of a gun or melee weapon that can play none of its own; its motions are from the hold.",
